##) SYNOPSIS:
==nmvn== **\<command-options\>**
manage multi-project maven worksets and versions

==nmvn== [**--version** <MVN_VERSION>] [{{args...}}]
==nmvn== **workset** [**list**|**path**|**get**|**set**|**add-root**|**remove-root**|**scan**|**edit**] [{{options...}}]
==nmvn== **version scan**    [**--workset** <FILE>] [**-j**|**--json**]
==nmvn== **version bump**    [**--workset** <FILE>] [**--dry**] [**--patch**|**--minor**|**--major**] [**-f**|**--force**] [**--cascade-references-only**|**--cascade-versions**] [**-a** <GA[#VER]>]...
==nmvn== **version update**  [**--workset** <FILE>] [**--dry**] [**-a** <GA#VER>]...
==nmvn== **version release** [**--workset** <FILE>] [**--dry**] [**--strict**] [**-a** <GA#VER>]...
==nmvn== **version check**   [**--workset** <FILE>] [**--fail-on-warning**] [**-j**|**--json**]

##) OPTIONS:

    ```sh -a <GA[#VER]> | -a=<GA[#VER]> | --artifact=<GA[#VER]>```
        specify target artifact and optional version using standard Nuts '#' delimiter (e.g. `com.example:mod1#1.1.0-SNAPSHOT`) or '=' delimiter (`com.example:mod1=1.1.0-SNAPSHOT`). For bump, omitting version auto-increments using the selected or default policy. Can be specified multiple times.

    ```sh --patch | --minor | --major```
        increment target artifact(s) or all workspace artifacts by patch, minor, or major.

    ```sh -f | --force```
        in bump mode, force advancing an artifact that is already in snapshot mode.

    ```sh --cascade-references-only```
        (default) update dependency, parent, and property references in consuming modules without changing their own project versions. If a consuming module was a release, it is automatically bumped to snapshot to preserve release immutability.

    ```sh --cascade-versions```
        cascade version bump through the dependency graph: updates references AND increments the project version of all direct and indirect dependents.

    ```sh --dry | -D```
        preview unified diff of changes without modifying files on disk. Default is non-dry (applies changes).

    ```sh --strict```
        in release mode, fail if any unmanaged external snapshot dependency is detected.

    ```sh -j | --json```
        output machine-readable JSON for CI/CD pipelines.

    ```sh --fail-on-warning```
        in check mode, fail with exit code 1 if any warnings are detected.

##) WORKFLOWS:

    **1. Start New Development Cycle (Post-Release Bump with Cascading Versions)**
    Bump released module `A` to snapshot and cascade to dependent modules `B`:
    ```sh nmvn version bump -a com.example:A --patch --cascade-versions --dry```
    ```sh nmvn version bump -a com.example:A --patch --cascade-versions```

    **2. Active Development Bump (Auto-Increment / Idempotent)**
    Bump module using semver flags without needing to calculate next version:
    ```sh nmvn version bump -a com.example:A --minor```
    ```sh nmvn version bump -a com.example:A --patch --force```

    **3. Strict Version Assignment / Dependency Alignment (`update`)**
    Update artifact to a strict version and align all references across workspace:
    ```sh nmvn version update -a net.thevpc.hl:hadra-lang#0.1.1```
    ```sh nmvn version update -a com.example:core#2.0.0-SNAPSHOT```

    **4. Synchronized / Lockstep Monorepo Bump**
    Bump all workspace modules together:
    ```sh nmvn version bump --minor```
    ```sh nmvn version bump -a com.example:core#2.0.0-SNAPSHOT -a com.example:client#2.0.0-SNAPSHOT```

    **5. Upstream Parent or BOM Upgrade**
    Update shared parent POM or BOM across child modules:
    ```sh nmvn version update -a com.example:company-parent#5.0.0```

    **6. Release Artifacts (Fix Snapshots)**
    Strip -SNAPSHOT from all workspace artifacts and convert references to release:
    ```sh nmvn version release --dry```
    ```sh nmvn version release --strict```
    ```sh nmvn version release -a com.example:core#1.0.0 -a com.example:client#1.0.0```

##) EXAMPLES:

```sh nmvn clean install```
   maven clean install

```sh nmvn workset add-root ../other-project --scan```
   add a root folder to current workset and scan discovered artifacts

```sh nmvn workset remove-root ../other-project --scan```
   remove a root folder from current workset and rescan

```sh nmvn workset list --recent```
   list recent worksets

```sh nmvn version scan```
   scan and print multi-project dependency graph

```sh nmvn version check```
   audit workspace for version discrepancies, mixed snapshot/releases, and cycles
